# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  docker-bridge — environment
#  Copy to `.env` (gitignored), then fill the required secret:
#
#    ./generate-secrets.sh          # creates .env and fills the bearer token in place
#
#  Named `env.example` without a leading dot because .gitignore blocks `.env.*`.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bearer token clients must present to the bridge. The bridge drives your
# authenticated Claude Code session, so this must not be blank.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY_API_KEY=

# Serve WITHOUT authentication. Leave false unless you specifically need it — for
# example to open /v1/models in a browser, which cannot send an Authorization
# header. An empty API key alone is NOT enough: the entrypoint refuses to start,
# so a key missing by accident can never silently open the bridge.
#
# With this true, any process that can reach the port drives your Claude Code
# session and spends against your account. Keep PROXY_BIND on 127.0.0.1.
#
#   ./generate-secrets.sh --allow-anonymous   # no token required
#   ./generate-secrets.sh --require-api-key   # token required again (tools untouched)
#   ./generate-secrets.sh --show-secrets      # also print the token to the shell
PROXY_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS=false

# ── Models ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default model when a request omits "model".
CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Advertised on GET /v1/models — this is what fills a client's model picker.
# Opus 5 first (the default); Fable 5 is the optional alternative. This is NOT a
# whitelist: with CLAUDE_CODE_PASS_MODEL=true any valid Claude model ID works.
CLAUDE_CODE_MODELS=claude-opus-5,claude-fable-5,claude-opus-4-8,claude-opus-4-7,claude-opus-4-6,claude-sonnet-5,claude-sonnet-4-6,claude-haiku-4-5,claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# Honour the client's requested model rather than forcing the default. Set false
# to pin every request to CLAUDE_CODE_PROXY_MODEL regardless of what's asked.
CLAUDE_CODE_PASS_MODEL=true

# Reasoning effort: low | medium | high | xhigh | max
CLAUDE_CODE_EFFORT=high

# ── Guardrails ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tools the agent may never use. The bridge sends this on every request, so it is
# enforced live — not just seeded into a settings file.
#
# To use EVERY tool, this must be EMPTY. Clearing CLAUDE_CODE_ALLOWED_TOOLS alone
# does nothing: an empty allow list means "no explicit allowlist", and the deny
# list below still wins. Shortcut: ./generate-secrets.sh --all-tools
CLAUDE_CODE_DISALLOWED_TOOLS=Bash,Edit,Write,NotebookEdit
# Empty = allow whatever isn't denied above (NOT "allow everything").
CLAUDE_CODE_ALLOWED_TOOLS=
CLAUDE_CODE_PERMISSION_MODE=dontAsk
# Per-invocation spend ceiling, in USD.
CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_BUDGET_USD=5.00

# ── Ports and binds ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Loopback on purpose. Change to 0.0.0.0 only if you understand that anyone who
# can reach the port can drive your Claude Code session.
PROXY_BIND=127.0.0.1
PROXY_PORT=18181

# ── Images and resources ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `latest` tracks the current Claude Code release; pin (e.g. 2.1.205) for repeatability.
CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=latest
NODE_BASE=node:22-bookworm-slim
MEMORY=2g
CPUS=1

# ── Host identity for the bind mount ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The container runs as this uid:gid so it can read AND refresh the bind-mounted
# ~/.claude. generate-secrets.sh fills these from `id -u` / `id -g`.
# HOST_UID=
# HOST_GID=

# ── Claude Code authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# A long-lived token from `claude setup-token`. NOT the default — use it only for CI
# or a host with no Claude Code login. It authenticates completions; it changes
# nothing about tools. claude.ai CONNECTORS (Slack, Drive, Gmail, Atlassian) are
# unavailable through this bridge either way: `claude -p` activates no MCP servers.
# See README, "Tool calling".
#
#   ./generate-secrets.sh --setup-token          # mint and store one
#   ./generate-secrets.sh --oauth-token sk-...   # store one you already have
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ── Which host directory to bind-mount ───────────────────────────────────────
# The container mounts these read-WRITE and runs as HOST_UID:HOST_GID, so it is the
# same Claude Code installation your host uses — one shared configuration, not a
# copy. Nothing here is destroyed by `docker compose down -v`.
#
#   HOST_CLAUDE_DIR=$HOME/.claude
#   HOST_CLAUDE_JSON=$HOME/.claude.json
#
# macOS: the live token is in the Keychain and the on-disk file goes stale, so
# generate-secrets.sh rewrites it from the Keychain on every run — same session, no
# re-login. Opt out with --no-host-token.
#
# Windows / CI: point HOST_CLAUDE_DIR at a directory holding a valid
# .credentials.json, or use CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN above (no connectors).

# ── Images from clients (Hermes screenshots, etc.) ───────────────────────────
# Clients pass a HOST path and expect the agent to Read it, so the cache is mounted
# at the SAME absolute path inside the container and handed to the CLI via --add-dir.
# Inline base64 images are not supported — see README, "Images".
#
#   HOST_COMPOSER_IMAGES=$HOME/Library/Application Support/Hermes/composer-images
#   HOST_IMAGE_CACHE=$HOME/.hermes/image_cache
#   CLAUDE_CODE_ADDITIONAL_DIRS=<comma-separated list of the above>
#
# Hermes DESKTOP writes pasted screenshots to composer-images, not to ~/.hermes.
#
# CLAUDE_CODE_APPEND_SYSTEM_PROMPT — the guardrail prompt. Derived from the tool
# posture by default; the upstream default wrongly says "use only explicitly allowed
# tools", which makes the model refuse when all tools are in fact permitted.

# ── Optional: corporate proxy pass-through ───────────────────────────────────
# HTTP_PROXY=
# HTTPS_PROXY=
# NO_PROXY=
